<title>FRANCE: French social security in red until 1999 - report.</title>
<headline>French social security in red until 1999 - report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's social security regime will be in the red until 1999, according to forecasts by the government, daily La Tribune Desfosses said on Friday.</p>
<p>The social security regime would be in the red again, as already predicted, in 1997 and in 1998 it will also produce a deficit of 12.3 billion before turning in a forecast surplus of 7.9 billion francs in 1999, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The government had already predicted a deficit in 1997, to the tune of 29.7 billion francs, after an expected deficit of 51.5 billion francs for this year.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
